 "frame": "audience",
 "note": "KeyCode Arena: the full house rig. Eight trusses' worth of kit on one universe -- a 16-lamp wash bar upstage, six uplight pods on the deck, eight beam spots on the mid truss, six zooming washes out front, four audience blinders with a strobe outboard of each end, two lasers, and a vertical pixel strip framing each side. Positions in metres in the AUDIENCE frame: at = [x, depth, height], +x = the audience's right, depth grows toward the audience, height from the floor.\n\nTHREE THINGS ARE DELIBERATE. Every device type here except the laser was read out of a real GDTF file under mvr/gdtf/ -- channel orders, beam angles and zoom ranges are the manufacturers' own, not invented. The lamps that mix colour and stay put number 24, a multiple of four, because groupsOf() splits inner/outer at floor(n/2) and an odd split makes every mirrored look lopsided. And unlike club16 this rig genuinely has DEPTH: the back truss sits at 0.0 and the front truss at 4.4, so a travelling effect crosses the room rather than running along a single bar.",
